# Microchip_TC1262_33VDB — component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint,
# LCSC pinned in properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields).
#
# 3.3 V LDO, 500 mA, SOT-223. Replaces the second buck on the logic chain
# (Ben, 2026-09-04): the 3.3 V rail draws about 105 mA, so a 5 V to 3.3 V buck
# was a whole converter cell - inductor, catch diode, feedback divider - for
# 0.35 W of delivered power.
#
# WHY THIS PART: the drop is 1.7 V, so at 150 mA of budget it burns 0.255 W in a
# 100 °C worst-case case ambient. That rules out SOT-23-5 (about 200 K/W, which
# would put the junction near 150 °C) and makes the SOT-223 tab the requirement,
# not a preference. LAYOUT MUST give the tab a generous pour: at ~70 K/W the
# junction sits near 118 °C against the 125 °C limit, and a bigger pour buys
# margin directly. Also chosen for 130 uA quiescent (an AMS1117-class part draws
# 2-12 mA continuously, which is 2-10% of this board's whole logic budget) and
# for ceramic-output stability, so it needs no tantalum.
#
# CAVEAT: 6 V absolute maximum input. It is fed from the regulated 5 V rail,
# whose worst case is about 5.1 V with 1% divider tolerance, so the margin is
# ~0.9 V. A 5 V rail fault takes this part with it - as it would the rest of the
# 3.3 V load either way.
# Pinned 2026-09-04: LCSC C52507, Extended, 1386 in stock.

VIN = io("VIN", Net, optional = True)
VOUT = io("VOUT", Net, optional = True)
GND = io("GND", Ground, optional = True)

Component(
    name = "Microchip_TC1262_33VDB",
    footprint = File("Microchip_TC1262_33VDB/SOT-223_L6.5-W3.5-P2.30-LS7.0-BR.kicad_mod"),
    symbol = Symbol("Microchip_TC1262_33VDB/TC1262-3.3VDB.kicad_sym"),
    prefix = "U",
    part = Part(mpn = "TC1262-3.3VDBTR", manufacturer = "Microchip"),
    properties = {"LCSC": "C52507", "MPN": "TC1262-3.3VDBTR"},
    pins = {
        "VIN": VIN,
        "VOUT": VOUT,
        "GND": GND,
    },
)
